# Build output. `node build-iray.mjs` regenerates all of this in under a second.
#
# iray.asm is deliberately NOT ignored: the build script emits assembly, so diffing the
# generated .asm between commits is how we see what a JS change actually did to the
# machine code and to the memory map. Both bugs found so far were address-layout bugs
# invisible in the JS diff, so that churn earns its keep. The disk image and the raw
# binary are opaque and change every build, so they stay out.
*.d64
iray.prg
iray-c.prg
iray-charset.bin

# Diagnostic builds (PX/PY/PA/SPIN/NORAY/...) emit here instead of iray.asm, so a
# throwaway start position or `inc pa` never lands in the tracked reference copy.
iray.diag.asm

# Local-only agent/editor settings (settings.json is shared and IS tracked)
.claude/settings.local.json
orbdiag.json

# macOS finder droppings
.DS_Store
cellscan.json
model.json
# charset-plan.json is TRACKED. It looks derived and it is not: it is the k-medians fit over a
# 2M-position scan of a shape-rich maze, it is canonical input to every build, and no level's map
# is an input to it. Untracked, a clean clone would silently refit the charset against whatever
# map happened to be built and ship different glyphs.
# Regenerate deliberately with:
#   CELLSCAN=1 CELLSTEP=0.2 CELLANG=1 node build-iray.mjs && node charsetgen.mjs

# fit-angel.mjs previews: regenerate with `node fit-angel.mjs TMP-3.d64 hangl1`. The FITTED
# asset (angel-face.json) is committed because the build reads it; the PNGs are just for looking.
hangl*-fit.png
hangl*-compare*.png

# fit-orb / fit-face / ang6 previews. Same rule as above and it is worth stating plainly,
# because the directory does not make it obvious which PNGs matter: a file the BUILD READS is
# an asset and is committed (sphere-*.png, angel-full.png); everything else here is a picture
# regenerated by a tool to be looked at once, and is reproducible from the committed input.
*-fit.png
*-flip.png
*-preq.png
*-free.png
*-joint*.png
*-dither-old.png
*-compare*.png
orb-*.png
ang6-*.png
vice-screen-*.png
.lvl2-tables.json
# the WALLOFF=1 subprocess dump, same as above
.wall-tables.json
# one per resident level, written by the per-level subprocess builds
.lvl1-tables.json
.lvl3-tables.json
.lvl*-tables.json
.wall*-tables.json

# fit-ram.mjs previews, same rule as the others above
ram-sprite-*.png
ram-sprites-all*.png
ram-sweep.png
CLEANUP-REVIEW.md

# compact.mjs's inputs and output. build-iray.mjs writes the first three each run (the RAM
# buffer sizes, the page-alignment requirements, and the level region to keep clear) and
# compact.mjs writes the fourth. Same rule as the .d64: regenerated in under a second, and a
# stale copy of any of them would relayout the image against a build that no longer exists.
iray.aligned.json
iray.bufsizes.json
iray.reserve.json
iray.compact.asm
tools/node_modules/
tools/package-lock.json
tools/.ship/
zz-vprof.d64
zz-pix.d64
